-<div class="faq-item__a font-PPFraktionMono" hidden=""><p data-type="body">Yes, and it’s one of the more common briefs our commercial structural engineers receive. Rooftop plant additions, new mezzanines, floor loading upgrades for changed use, and additional storeys all require the existing structure to be assessed before anything can be designed. The starting point is always the original structural drawings (if they exist). If they don’t, we work from a site inspection and measured survey to understand what’s there and how it’s performing.</p>
